1
00:00:33,346 --> 00:00:38,059
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

2
00:00:38,726 --> 00:00:39,936
‎Listen, Kim.

3
00:00:40,019 --> 00:00:42,438
‎Let's see each other more often, okay?

4
00:00:42,522 --> 00:00:44,190
‎Min-ji's grown up now.

5
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:45,775
‎He's right.
‎She'll have a boyfriend soon too.

6
00:00:45,859 --> 00:00:46,860
‎What the hell?

7
00:00:46,943 --> 00:00:47,777
‎What? You scared?

8
00:00:47,861 --> 00:00:49,070
<i>‎This has nothing to do with us.</i>

9
00:00:49,863 --> 00:00:52,282
<i>‎We're middle-aged men</i>
<i>‎who tolerate injustice.</i>

10
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:54,450
<i>‎We're no longer young.</i>

11
00:00:54,534 --> 00:00:56,786
<i>‎We're just middle-aged men with glasses.</i>

12
00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:58,204
‎Dad!

13
00:00:58,872 --> 00:00:59,998
‎I'm sorry.

14
00:01:00,081 --> 00:01:02,876
‎I've fallen short as a parent
‎since I'm raising her alone.

15
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:05,003
‎I ask that you find it in your heart
‎to forgive us.

16
00:01:05,086 --> 00:01:07,922
<i>‎I feel so angry, frustrated, and pathetic.</i>

17
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:09,382
‎I don't have a mom.

18
00:01:09,465 --> 00:01:10,884
‎You're all I have left.

19
00:01:10,967 --> 00:01:12,760
<i>‎They're the bad ones.</i>

20
00:01:13,303 --> 00:01:15,471
<i>‎I'm going to make you get on your knees.</i>

21
00:01:15,555 --> 00:01:17,098
‎Hit me. I said hit me!

22
00:01:17,182 --> 00:01:18,016
‎Just die!

23
00:01:18,099 --> 00:01:20,059
<i>‎My dad is Ju Gang-chan,</i>
<i>‎the chairman of Juhak Construction.</i>

24
00:01:20,143 --> 00:01:23,438
‎I'll pay whatever you want,
‎so just get rid of the body.

25
00:01:23,938 --> 00:01:27,275
‎I owe Chairman Ju,
‎so I'm making an exception to help you.

26
00:01:27,358 --> 00:01:28,985
<i>‎Let's keep this a secret from your father.</i>

27
00:01:29,068 --> 00:01:30,653
‎Did you meet Min-ji yesterday?

28
00:01:30,737 --> 00:01:32,530
<i>‎I only heard something</i>
<i>‎about the back gate.</i>

29
00:01:32,614 --> 00:01:33,448
<i>‎Can I ask a question?</i>

30
00:01:33,531 --> 00:01:35,700
<i>‎This is your hair tie, right?</i>

31
00:01:35,783 --> 00:01:38,161
<i>‎Hey, old man. You're dead meat.</i>

32
00:01:38,244 --> 00:01:40,455
‎Tell me. Where's Min-ji?

33
00:01:40,538 --> 00:01:41,497
<i>‎Oh Min-cheol…</i>

34
00:01:41,581 --> 00:01:43,750
<i>‎I'm only keeping you alive</i>
<i>‎because I believe my daughter is.</i>

35
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:47,295
‎If she's not, you, your friends,
‎and your family will all die.

36
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:49,923
<i>‎I took care of the girl's body.</i>

37
00:01:50,006 --> 00:01:51,799
‎Don't answer it,
‎and get rid of that phone.

38
00:01:51,883 --> 00:01:53,051
‎UNABLE TO ACCESS CONVERSATION

39
00:01:53,134 --> 00:01:54,135
<i>‎Contact them now.</i>

40
00:01:54,844 --> 00:01:56,596
‎A tier-one wanted fugitive
‎has been caught on camera.

41
00:01:57,096 --> 00:02:01,893
<i>‎Go to the South and bring me back</i>
<i>‎the head of the fake Number 66.</i>

42
00:02:01,976 --> 00:02:02,936
<i>‎Director, we have a situation.</i>

43
00:02:03,019 --> 00:02:05,355
‎We can't hand over someone
‎as dangerous as Kim to the North.

44
00:02:05,438 --> 00:02:06,564
<i>‎We'll get to him first.</i>

45
00:02:06,648 --> 00:02:08,149
‎Have you heard from Kim?

46
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:09,275
‎I'll try calling him.

47
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:11,194
‎It's a dead body!

48
00:02:11,277 --> 00:02:14,155
‎You should've at least
‎covered it with plastic, idiot!

49
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:16,908
‎"Access denied"?

50
00:02:16,991 --> 00:02:18,534
‎I'll try it again.

51
00:02:19,244 --> 00:02:20,286
‎Does that belong to him?

52
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:21,579
‎Yes, sir. We confiscated it.

53
00:02:22,205 --> 00:02:23,039
‎"My daughter"?

54
00:02:28,294 --> 00:02:31,506
‎5 MONTHS AGO

55
00:02:34,842 --> 00:02:35,677
‎Hey.

56
00:02:42,684 --> 00:02:43,559
‎Damn it.

57
00:02:46,312 --> 00:02:47,146
‎Move.

58
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,773
‎Watch where you're going.

59
00:02:50,483 --> 00:02:52,527
‎What a bitch.

60
00:02:53,194 --> 00:02:54,445
‎Hey, Min-ji.

61
00:02:54,529 --> 00:02:55,613
‎Lend me your phone.

62
00:02:55,697 --> 00:02:58,616
‎I got caught playing games,
‎so they took my phone. I'm so annoyed.

63
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,785
‎I can't. What about me, then?

64
00:03:00,868 --> 00:03:03,913
‎I'll give it back
‎right after fourth period.

65
00:03:03,997 --> 00:03:05,623
‎Come on, we're friends.

66
00:03:05,707 --> 00:03:07,583
‎We're best friends!

67
00:03:10,753 --> 00:03:12,505
‎-Just until fourth period.
‎-Okay.

68
00:03:12,588 --> 00:03:13,464
‎Thank you.

69
00:03:15,341 --> 00:03:16,175
‎Hey.

70
00:03:17,051 --> 00:03:18,845
‎What's with the crappy phone?

71
00:03:19,637 --> 00:03:21,431
‎Get a new one already.
‎This looks like my dad's.

72
00:03:22,515 --> 00:03:23,349
‎Thank you.

73
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:26,227
‎Look at what I got.

74
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:27,145
‎-What?
‎-What is it?

75
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:28,104
‎It's pretty, right?

76
00:03:28,604 --> 00:03:29,647
‎I don't like the color.

77
00:03:30,565 --> 00:03:31,733
‎It's not my style.

78
00:03:31,816 --> 00:03:34,068
‎-Nothing beats the latest model.
‎-It's pretty.

79
00:03:34,152 --> 00:03:36,612
‎-You know, I bet mine's more expensive.
‎-It's the latest model.

80
00:03:36,696 --> 00:03:38,656
‎EPISODE 3

81
00:03:39,574 --> 00:03:40,783
‎Dad, let's eat.

82
00:03:41,909 --> 00:03:42,744
‎Dad!

83
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:49,584
‎What's all this?

84
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:50,752
‎Did you make this?

85
00:03:50,835 --> 00:03:52,420
‎Yeah. Here, cool off in front of the fan.

86
00:03:52,503 --> 00:03:53,629
‎It's hot, isn't it?

87
00:03:54,255 --> 00:03:57,133
‎I may not be good at studying,
‎but I make a great spicy stir-fried pork.

88
00:03:57,884 --> 00:03:58,760
‎Thanks.

89
00:04:03,723 --> 00:04:04,724
‎Why aren't you eating?

90
00:04:04,807 --> 00:04:07,310
‎Because adults are supposed to eat first.

91
00:04:15,526 --> 00:04:17,653
‎Is everything okay at work?

92
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:18,780
‎-Yeah.
‎-Everything good?

93
00:04:19,947 --> 00:04:21,366
‎Do you need anything?

94
00:04:22,283 --> 00:04:23,117
‎No.

95
00:04:24,744 --> 00:04:26,954
‎I'm going to the convenience store later.

96
00:04:27,038 --> 00:04:27,997
‎Do you want anything?

97
00:04:28,664 --> 00:04:29,499
‎No, I'm okay.

98
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:32,794
‎You've had a long day.
‎How about a massage later?

99
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:35,004
‎I'm fine.

100
00:04:36,714 --> 00:04:38,633
‎I'll at least do the dishes, then.

101
00:04:38,716 --> 00:04:41,010
‎It's too much for you to do alone,
‎and I'm all grown up now.

102
00:04:43,971 --> 00:04:44,806
‎How much do you need?

103
00:04:48,393 --> 00:04:49,977
‎I don't want money.

104
00:04:50,061 --> 00:04:50,895
‎I want a new phone.

105
00:04:53,189 --> 00:04:54,065
‎Is it broken?

106
00:04:54,774 --> 00:04:57,860
‎No, but I've used it for over three years,
‎so it'll probably die soon.

107
00:05:00,446 --> 00:05:01,614
‎Tell me when it dies.

108
00:05:03,574 --> 00:05:06,035
‎No one uses their phone
‎until it dies these days.

109
00:05:06,119 --> 00:05:08,162
‎The other kids get a new phone every year.

110
00:05:08,246 --> 00:05:09,372
‎No, not even a year.

111
00:05:09,455 --> 00:05:10,998
‎Some kids get a new one every month.

112
00:05:12,125 --> 00:05:13,209
‎Want to see my phone?

113
00:05:14,252 --> 00:05:16,212
‎Look at this.
‎How can I take this to school?

114
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:17,588
‎It's so embarrassing.

115
00:05:17,672 --> 00:05:18,923
‎It totally sucks.

116
00:05:30,476 --> 00:05:32,186
‎Or at least get a new one for yourself.

117
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:34,063
‎Forget it. I'm eating in my room.

118
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:41,654
‎Kim Min-ji!

119
00:05:41,737 --> 00:05:43,030
‎It wasn't me.

120
00:05:43,114 --> 00:05:44,448
‎It was the wind.

121
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:01,507
‎-I'm home.
‎-Hey.

122
00:06:16,606 --> 00:06:18,524
‎Oh my gosh! What's this?

123
00:06:21,027 --> 00:06:22,028
‎Wait, it's that phone!

124
00:06:27,033 --> 00:06:27,992
‎Dad.

125
00:06:28,951 --> 00:06:29,911
‎I love you.

126
00:06:37,293 --> 00:06:38,628
‎I love you more.

127
00:06:50,097 --> 00:06:51,224
‎Why did he get me this?

128
00:06:57,772 --> 00:06:58,773
‎What's this?

129
00:06:58,856 --> 00:07:00,024
‎It's so tacky.

130
00:07:18,793 --> 00:07:20,253
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

131
00:07:26,217 --> 00:07:27,134
‎"My daughter"?

132
00:07:37,436 --> 00:07:38,396
‎What the hell?

133
00:07:49,407 --> 00:07:50,283
‎Hello?

134
00:07:52,159 --> 00:07:53,035
‎Is that you, Min-ji?

135
00:07:54,912 --> 00:07:55,746
‎Min-ji…

136
00:08:01,043 --> 00:08:02,169
<i>‎The phone you are calling is turned off.</i>

137
00:08:02,253 --> 00:08:04,547
<i>‎You will be redirected to voicemail,</i>

138
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:07,091
<i>‎and charges will apply after the beep.</i>

139
00:08:29,572 --> 00:08:30,740
‎Have you located him?

140
00:08:31,532 --> 00:08:32,450
‎We're still looking.

141
00:08:32,533 --> 00:08:34,702
‎Why is it taking so long
‎to trace his phone?

142
00:08:35,202 --> 00:08:36,954
‎We can't get into the data on the phone,

143
00:08:37,038 --> 00:08:39,540
‎so tracking it by frequency alone
‎will take a while.

144
00:08:44,712 --> 00:08:46,297
‎MY DAUGHTER

145
00:08:48,591 --> 00:08:50,092
<i>‎The phone you are calling is turned off.</i>

146
00:08:50,176 --> 00:08:51,510
<i>‎You will be redirected to voicemail.</i>

147
00:08:52,470 --> 00:08:54,639
<i>‎If he's caught on and fled,</i>

148
00:08:54,722 --> 00:08:56,766
<i>‎there's a chance he destroyed his phone.</i>

149
00:08:57,683 --> 00:08:59,518
‎Sir, can you go faster?

150
00:09:06,484 --> 00:09:07,610
‎Sir.

151
00:09:07,693 --> 00:09:11,113
‎We detected a background check
‎on Codename 66 by Hwasin Police Station.

152
00:09:14,784 --> 00:09:16,243
‎Head to the police station,

153
00:09:16,327 --> 00:09:18,245
‎and reassign the surveillance team
‎to tracking detail.

154
00:09:18,329 --> 00:09:20,122
‎-Yes, sir.
‎-Understood.

155
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,255
‎Should I put down last year
‎in the field here?

156
00:09:28,339 --> 00:09:29,840
‎-Yes, that's right.
‎-Okay.

157
00:09:40,851 --> 00:09:41,686
‎Okay.

158
00:09:49,944 --> 00:09:50,778
‎Sang-a.

159
00:09:51,696 --> 00:09:52,530
‎Where are you going?

160
00:09:53,906 --> 00:09:54,740
‎Where are you going?

161
00:09:57,410 --> 00:09:59,995
‎Wow, the coffee is great today.

162
00:10:05,626 --> 00:10:07,002
‎-I need to take this call.
‎-Sure.

163
00:10:10,923 --> 00:10:12,383
‎Hello?

164
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:13,884
‎Yes.

165
00:10:14,593 --> 00:10:16,846
‎All right, sure thing.

166
00:11:03,642 --> 00:11:04,852
‎Honey.

167
00:11:04,935 --> 00:11:07,438
‎Hye-ri refuses to come out of her room.

168
00:11:09,023 --> 00:11:10,524
‎She's skipping school today too?

169
00:11:10,608 --> 00:11:14,195
‎When I try to go in,
‎she gets mad and tells me to get out.

170
00:11:28,292 --> 00:11:30,377
<i>‎Do you happen to know</i>
<i>‎what her dad does for a living?</i>

171
00:11:30,461 --> 00:11:31,504
‎Why do you ask?

172
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:35,716
‎I don't know.

173
00:11:36,675 --> 00:11:38,135
‎I'm just curious.

174
00:11:42,973 --> 00:11:45,309
‎Find out what happened to Hye-ri.

175
00:11:45,392 --> 00:11:46,477
‎Yes, sir.

176
00:11:57,613 --> 00:11:59,198
‎JUHAK CONSTRUCTION CO., LTD.

177
00:12:05,204 --> 00:12:06,539
‎JU HYE-RI

178
00:12:11,377 --> 00:12:12,419
‎"Sung Min-ho."

179
00:12:12,503 --> 00:12:13,963
‎INCOMING, OUTGOING, MISSED

180
00:12:14,046 --> 00:12:15,297
‎Open the messages.

181
00:12:19,093 --> 00:12:21,053
‎I REALLY WORKED MY MUSCLES TODAY
‎SHOULD I DO A FITNESS SHOOT?

182
00:12:21,136 --> 00:12:22,846
‎DO WHATEVER, BUT MIND YOUR MANNERS
‎I'M AT SCHOOL, WASN'T EXPECTING THAT

183
00:12:22,930 --> 00:12:24,348
‎-LOL WHY? TOO HOT FOR YOU?
‎-UGH…

184
00:12:24,431 --> 00:12:25,391
‎I MISS YOU

185
00:12:25,474 --> 00:12:27,893
<i>‎-Min-ho, can you come here today?</i>
<i>‎-Yeah, what's up?</i>

186
00:12:27,977 --> 00:12:30,396
<i>‎There's this girl</i>
<i>‎who doesn't know her place,</i>

187
00:12:30,479 --> 00:12:32,022
<i>‎so I need to teach her a lesson.</i>

188
00:12:32,106 --> 00:12:33,023
<i>‎Bring the others too.</i>

189
00:12:33,107 --> 00:12:34,191
<i>‎Oh, so it's not because you miss me.</i>

190
00:12:34,275 --> 00:12:37,236
<i>‎Who's the bitch with the nerve</i>
<i>‎to mess with my Hye-ri?</i>

191
00:12:37,319 --> 00:12:38,612
<i>‎Her name is Kim Min-ji.</i>

192
00:12:38,696 --> 00:12:40,322
<i>‎She's got such an attitude</i>

193
00:12:40,406 --> 00:12:41,824
<i>‎and always talks back to me.</i>

194
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,867
<i>‎Okay, I'll be right there.</i>

195
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,870
<i>‎Damn it, I didn't sleep a wink.</i>

196
00:12:46,954 --> 00:12:48,414
<i>‎Why? Don't you trust me?</i>

197
00:12:48,497 --> 00:12:50,040
<i>‎I'll take care of everything.</i>

198
00:12:55,421 --> 00:12:57,840
‎SMH_UNTAMED: LOOKING PRETTY TODAY TOO

199
00:12:58,424 --> 00:12:59,675
‎Check Sung Min-ho's account.

200
00:12:59,758 --> 00:13:01,093
‎SUNG MIN-HO

201
00:13:20,946 --> 00:13:23,365
‎DOWON LAUNDRY

202
00:14:19,546 --> 00:14:21,465
‎STUDENT ID
‎KIM MIN-JI, SONGIN HIGH SCHOOL

203
00:14:33,769 --> 00:14:36,438
‎Comrade, did you find 66?

204
00:14:37,231 --> 00:14:38,482
‎Well, well.

205
00:14:39,566 --> 00:14:40,943
‎You said you were hungry,

206
00:14:41,986 --> 00:14:44,154
‎but it looks like you'll never eat again.

207
00:14:45,948 --> 00:14:47,282
‎A VP9?

208
00:14:48,325 --> 00:14:51,704
‎That thing won't go through a frying pan,
‎much less a person.

209
00:14:52,788 --> 00:14:53,706
‎Is that so?

210
00:14:58,752 --> 00:14:59,753
‎It went through.

211
00:15:07,469 --> 00:15:09,304
‎Rock and roll!

212
00:15:16,061 --> 00:15:18,188
‎Come on!

213
00:15:18,272 --> 00:15:19,481
‎You son of a bitch.

214
00:16:00,189 --> 00:16:01,648
‎Stop punching my stomach.

215
00:16:05,319 --> 00:16:06,528
‎That's just cheap.

216
00:16:07,404 --> 00:16:08,405
‎The gun!

217
00:16:08,489 --> 00:16:10,032
‎The gun, the gun!

218
00:16:23,128 --> 00:16:24,630
‎Hey, you bastard!

219
00:16:30,177 --> 00:16:31,011
‎What the hell?

220
00:16:33,639 --> 00:16:35,599
‎Oops, my knees.

221
00:16:36,642 --> 00:16:38,143
‎If I were ten years younger…

222
00:16:40,604 --> 00:16:41,605
‎Where is it?

223
00:16:42,856 --> 00:16:43,857
‎Oh, there it is.

224
00:17:10,509 --> 00:17:12,094
‎Man, this guy is something else.

225
00:17:12,594 --> 00:17:13,887
‎Hold on.

226
00:17:13,971 --> 00:17:15,430
‎I need to call Kim.

227
00:17:15,514 --> 00:17:16,723
‎I need to let him know.

228
00:17:18,016 --> 00:17:21,395
‎Damn it, the police confiscated my phone!

229
00:17:31,822 --> 00:17:33,157
‎This is insane.

230
00:17:38,662 --> 00:17:42,040
‎Jeez, that was a brutal fight.
‎They're so barbaric.

231
00:17:42,124 --> 00:17:44,418
‎How could they do that
‎in someone else's house?

232
00:17:47,629 --> 00:17:49,381
‎And why did he take off the fridge door?

233
00:17:58,390 --> 00:18:01,393
‎This means Kim was arrested by the police.

234
00:18:01,935 --> 00:18:02,936
‎Does that make any sense?

235
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:05,689
‎There's no other reason for his
‎background check record to show up.

236
00:18:08,317 --> 00:18:10,611
‎No matter how I look at it,
‎it just doesn't add up.

237
00:18:14,489 --> 00:18:15,616
‎Talk to me.

238
00:18:15,699 --> 00:18:18,744
‎Someone is after Agent Kim.

239
00:18:18,827 --> 00:18:20,954
‎I think it's a North Korean operative.

240
00:18:21,038 --> 00:18:21,955
‎Already?

241
00:18:22,039 --> 00:18:23,582
‎And Park Jin-cheol

242
00:18:23,665 --> 00:18:25,834
‎showed up at the scene.

243
00:18:25,918 --> 00:18:30,172
‎Even Park Jin-cheol?
‎What game are these bastards playing?

244
00:18:30,255 --> 00:18:33,508
<i>‎Sir, we have a location</i>
<i>‎on Agent Kim's phone.</i>

245
00:18:33,592 --> 00:18:36,011
‎Where? Is it at Hwasin Police Station?

246
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:39,056
‎No, sir.

247
00:18:40,849 --> 00:18:43,185
‎GPS reads N99, E81.

248
00:18:43,268 --> 00:18:45,020
‎-It's Pure Taekwondo.
‎-It's a Taekwondo studio, sir.

249
00:18:47,814 --> 00:18:49,107
<i>‎Taekwondo master, Sung Han-soo.</i>

250
00:18:49,858 --> 00:18:51,693
<i>‎Former Olympic gold medalist in Taekwondo.</i>

251
00:18:51,777 --> 00:18:53,028
<i>‎Three-time consecutive world champion.</i>

252
00:18:54,029 --> 00:18:56,156
<i>‎After retiring,</i>
<i>‎he was recruited by the government</i>

253
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:59,409
<i>‎and infiltrated the North</i>
<i>‎with Agent Kim and Park Jin-cheol.</i>

254
00:19:00,702 --> 00:19:02,329
‎SUNG HAN-SOO
‎NIS SPECIAL RECRUIT

255
00:19:02,412 --> 00:19:04,164
‎Roundhouse kick! One!

256
00:19:05,374 --> 00:19:06,500
‎Two!

257
00:19:07,709 --> 00:19:09,253
‎Nice and clean! Three!

258
00:19:10,254 --> 00:19:11,838
‎Switch feet!

259
00:19:12,339 --> 00:19:13,340
‎One!

260
00:19:14,508 --> 00:19:15,509
‎Two!

261
00:19:20,931 --> 00:19:22,224
‎-Instructor Choi.
‎-Yes, sir.

262
00:19:22,307 --> 00:19:23,517
‎Can you take the kids for <i>‎gubo</i>‎?

263
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:25,060
‎What does <i>‎gubo</i>‎ mean?

264
00:19:25,143 --> 00:19:26,103
‎It's just running.

265
00:19:26,186 --> 00:19:27,354
‎-Let's go, kids.
‎-Go for a run.

266
00:19:27,437 --> 00:19:28,689
‎-Okay!
‎-Okay!

267
00:19:40,659 --> 00:19:42,953
‎I was so surprised
‎that I didn't even know how to react.

268
00:19:43,036 --> 00:19:43,870
‎What's going on?

269
00:19:43,954 --> 00:19:47,291
‎You wouldn't have come all the way here
‎if it wasn't a big deal.

270
00:19:48,709 --> 00:19:50,544
‎-I need the bunker.
‎-The bunker?

271
00:19:50,627 --> 00:19:53,171
‎Did someone steal your bank book
‎and take off or something?

272
00:19:53,755 --> 00:19:54,756
‎Min-ji…

273
00:19:55,424 --> 00:19:56,800
‎What about her?

274
00:19:59,845 --> 00:20:00,971
‎I read a message

275
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,348
‎saying she was dead.

276
00:20:05,309 --> 00:20:06,810
‎-What did you say?
‎-But then,

277
00:20:07,644 --> 00:20:08,562
‎I got a call.

278
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:12,316
‎What are you talking about?

279
00:20:12,399 --> 00:20:14,318
‎Explain it so I can understand!

280
00:20:14,401 --> 00:20:15,861
‎You don't even know if she's alive?

281
00:20:15,944 --> 00:20:16,987
‎Where is she right now?

282
00:20:17,571 --> 00:20:20,490
‎All I know is that she was kidnapped.

283
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,993
‎I got a call, but I couldn't answer it.

284
00:20:25,162 --> 00:20:27,914
‎I need to get rid of this right now,
‎but I can't.

285
00:20:27,998 --> 00:20:29,374
‎Get rid of it? Why?

286
00:20:30,959 --> 00:20:32,252
‎Did you get into trouble?

287
00:20:35,172 --> 00:20:37,215
‎They're probably tracking me already.

288
00:20:42,304 --> 00:20:45,140
‎I'm sorry for bringing you into this.

289
00:20:47,976 --> 00:20:48,935
‎Han-soo.

290
00:20:55,650 --> 00:20:57,778
‎Let's trace Min-ji's phone first.

291
00:21:19,841 --> 00:21:22,552
‎Wow, look who it is.

292
00:21:24,721 --> 00:21:26,598
‎Someone who'd be in a bind
‎if they ran into me.

293
00:21:27,224 --> 00:21:30,185
‎Master, a monster caught me.

294
00:21:33,313 --> 00:21:34,231
‎Let's see here.

295
00:21:35,357 --> 00:21:37,192
‎Is there someone
‎in an even bigger bind inside?

296
00:21:39,403 --> 00:21:43,073
‎Are you washed-up agents
‎reminiscing about the good old days?

297
00:21:43,156 --> 00:21:44,574
‎Let the kid go.

298
00:21:50,038 --> 00:21:50,914
‎Hey, Taekwondo.

299
00:21:51,623 --> 00:21:52,874
‎Stay out of this.

300
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:55,502
‎You're a South Korean citizen,
‎so I'll let you off the hook.

301
00:21:55,585 --> 00:21:56,837
‎But Kim…

302
00:21:57,629 --> 00:21:58,463
‎I mean…

303
00:21:59,423 --> 00:22:02,092
‎North Korean-born 66 is different.

304
00:22:02,717 --> 00:22:04,428
‎That bastard violated the contract.

305
00:22:04,511 --> 00:22:06,388
‎He's exposed himself to the North,

306
00:22:07,097 --> 00:22:07,931
‎is what I'm saying.

307
00:22:09,099 --> 00:22:10,976
‎Let me go, monster!

308
00:22:11,059 --> 00:22:12,102
‎Hey, kid.

309
00:22:12,185 --> 00:22:15,313
‎The real monster is your master.
‎Just look at him.

310
00:22:15,397 --> 00:22:17,065
‎Gosh, he's scary.

311
00:22:17,149 --> 00:22:19,860
‎That's a lie! Master, run!

312
00:22:25,115 --> 00:22:26,491
‎It's a monster!

313
00:23:01,443 --> 00:23:03,361
‎Two blank rounds.
‎You haven't changed a bit.

314
00:23:06,239 --> 00:23:08,533
‎It could be three. Want to shoot and see?

315
00:23:32,265 --> 00:23:33,934
‎Go around to the emergency exit.

316
00:23:34,017 --> 00:23:35,018
‎The emergency exit!

317
00:23:49,699 --> 00:23:50,575
‎Open the door!

318
00:24:36,413 --> 00:24:37,414
‎Step aside.

319
00:24:37,497 --> 00:24:38,331
‎Ready.

320
00:24:43,420 --> 00:24:44,754
‎-Three!
‎-Four!

321
00:24:44,838 --> 00:24:45,880
‎Stand down.

322
00:24:46,881 --> 00:24:47,841
‎Go after them!

323
00:24:47,924 --> 00:24:48,842
‎Agent Jang, this way!

324
00:24:49,968 --> 00:24:52,053
‎PURE TAEKWONDO

325
00:25:33,345 --> 00:25:34,304
‎Hey.

326
00:25:41,019 --> 00:25:43,355
‎I hope this still works.

327
00:25:51,196 --> 00:25:52,405
‎There we go.

328
00:25:53,323 --> 00:25:54,157
‎It's working.

329
00:25:56,785 --> 00:25:58,161
‎It's been a while. Can you still manage?

330
00:25:58,244 --> 00:26:01,373
‎You don't forget how to use your fists
‎just because it's been a while, do you?

331
00:26:04,209 --> 00:26:05,293
‎I'm sorry.

332
00:26:05,377 --> 00:26:07,712
‎Now the SMD is on you because of me.

333
00:26:07,796 --> 00:26:11,049
‎If Tae-hun were in the same situation,
‎I'd have gone to you first too.

334
00:26:13,301 --> 00:26:15,011
‎Did you forget how to drive?

335
00:26:15,095 --> 00:26:16,971
‎Hurry up. Let's go find Min-ji.

336
00:26:30,944 --> 00:26:34,280
‎ONCE A MARINE, ALWAYS A MARINE
‎KOREAN MARINE VETERANS FEDERATION

337
00:26:34,364 --> 00:26:35,365
‎Salute!

338
00:26:43,581 --> 00:26:45,333
‎Come on, hurry up.

339
00:26:46,668 --> 00:26:48,128
‎They'll catch up with us soon.

340
00:26:48,711 --> 00:26:49,754
‎Did you tap into the tower yet?

341
00:26:49,838 --> 00:26:52,924
‎Frequency isn't locking,
‎so I'm pulling wide-area data instead.

342
00:27:05,395 --> 00:27:06,729
‎Who is it?

343
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:08,523
‎It's an unknown number.

344
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:10,984
‎It could be Min-ji.

345
00:27:12,444 --> 00:27:14,320
‎Give it to me. You just focus on driving.

346
00:27:15,864 --> 00:27:16,948
‎-Hello--
<i>‎-You punk!</i>

347
00:27:17,031 --> 00:27:18,575
<i>‎You're in big trouble!</i>

348
00:27:18,658 --> 00:27:20,493
<i>‎Some guy from the North came to kill you.</i>

349
00:27:20,577 --> 00:27:21,411
<i>‎Be careful.</i>

350
00:27:21,494 --> 00:27:23,329
‎I should've ended him myself, but…

351
00:27:23,955 --> 00:27:25,165
‎I'm sorry.

352
00:27:25,248 --> 00:27:26,958
‎I couldn't jump because I have bad knees.

353
00:27:27,041 --> 00:27:28,543
‎Anyway, that's not important right now.

354
00:27:29,169 --> 00:27:30,211
‎Min-ji will be in danger too.

355
00:27:30,295 --> 00:27:32,255
<i>‎Where's Min-ji's school?</i>
<i>‎I'll go there right now.</i>

356
00:27:32,839 --> 00:27:33,840
<i>‎Are you listening?</i>

357
00:27:33,923 --> 00:27:35,842
‎Hey! Are you listening to me?!

358
00:27:35,925 --> 00:27:38,636
‎-Jeez, it's as if he's on speaker.
<i>‎-Hey, you punk!</i>

359
00:27:41,139 --> 00:27:43,933
‎Hey, where are you? How did you get out?

360
00:27:44,017 --> 00:27:45,018
‎Oh, you're with him.

361
00:27:45,101 --> 00:27:46,644
‎I needed some air, so I came out.

362
00:27:47,228 --> 00:27:50,523
‎You crazy bastard.
‎You can't just leave lockup for some air.

363
00:27:50,607 --> 00:27:51,900
<i>‎That's not the issue here.</i>

364
00:27:51,983 --> 00:27:53,860
‎Let's go to Min-ji right now.
‎Where's her school?

365
00:27:53,943 --> 00:27:56,863
‎-She's not at school.
<i>‎-Why?</i>

366
00:27:59,616 --> 00:28:00,909
‎We think she's been kidnapped.

367
00:28:00,992 --> 00:28:02,452
‎What?!

368
00:28:02,535 --> 00:28:04,579
‎Who's the goddamn bastard?!

369
00:28:04,662 --> 00:28:06,414
‎Let's talk more in person.

370
00:28:06,498 --> 00:28:09,918
‎I'll send you the location once I have it,
‎so get over there right away.

371
00:28:10,001 --> 00:28:11,085
‎Hold on.

372
00:28:11,169 --> 00:28:12,295
‎I found it.

373
00:28:13,296 --> 00:28:14,339
‎Where is it?

374
00:28:15,882 --> 00:28:16,883
‎Got the location.

375
00:28:17,842 --> 00:28:21,804
‎It's 8-3, Gongdan-gil, Seonmin-eup,
‎Gangjang-si, Gyeonggi-do.

376
00:28:24,516 --> 00:28:27,060
‎Okay, I'll meet you there.

377
00:28:32,649 --> 00:28:33,650
‎Thank you for your phone, sir.

378
00:28:36,069 --> 00:28:37,862
‎-Salute!
‎-Salute!

379
00:28:39,489 --> 00:28:41,241
‎I'll make sure to repay this favor soon.

380
00:28:41,324 --> 00:28:42,367
‎It was nothing.

381
00:28:42,450 --> 00:28:45,328
‎Just buy me a coffee from there, then.

382
00:28:45,411 --> 00:28:46,871
‎Oh, coffee.

383
00:28:46,955 --> 00:28:49,916
‎Oh, but I left my wallet in lockup.

384
00:28:49,999 --> 00:28:53,086
‎May I offer this instead of coffee?

385
00:29:05,306 --> 00:29:07,141
‎-This is tasty.
‎-Right?

386
00:29:07,225 --> 00:29:08,560
‎This is the next best thing to coffee.

387
00:29:09,310 --> 00:29:12,021
‎Then could you lend me money
‎for transportation, sir?

388
00:29:12,605 --> 00:29:13,648
‎-Transportation money?
‎-Yes, sir.

389
00:29:13,731 --> 00:29:15,233
‎I'd really appreciate it, sir.

390
00:29:52,645 --> 00:29:53,730
‎Who is it?

391
00:30:07,994 --> 00:30:09,120
‎So you're saying

392
00:30:09,871 --> 00:30:12,206
‎that girl's father did this to you.

393
00:30:17,712 --> 00:30:19,380
‎He was scary as hell.

394
00:30:20,006 --> 00:30:22,050
‎I'm telling you, he isn't human.

395
00:30:22,675 --> 00:30:24,260
‎His body

396
00:30:24,344 --> 00:30:27,347
‎is freaking covered in scars
‎and bullet wounds!

397
00:30:27,931 --> 00:30:31,225
‎Goddamn it. You know whose fault it is
‎that I'm going through this hell?

398
00:30:31,309 --> 00:30:33,561
‎It's all because of Hye-ri!

399
00:30:36,397 --> 00:30:38,232
‎You seem pretty capable.

400
00:30:38,316 --> 00:30:40,777
‎Ask the higher-ups for more money.

401
00:30:49,577 --> 00:30:51,329
<i>‎You're saying Hye-ri's involved?</i>

402
00:30:52,205 --> 00:30:53,373
‎Yes, sir.

403
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:56,918
‎Okay.

404
00:30:57,877 --> 00:30:59,420
‎Get rid of any evidence first.

405
00:31:00,380 --> 00:31:01,214
<i>‎Yes, sir.</i>

406
00:31:09,806 --> 00:31:11,891
‎I assume you have no way

407
00:31:12,517 --> 00:31:16,229
‎of contacting the person
‎who took Min-ji's body.

408
00:31:19,232 --> 00:31:21,609
‎I seriously don't know.

409
00:31:25,780 --> 00:31:26,823
‎You don't know, huh?

410
00:32:18,041 --> 00:32:19,417
‎Come on, let's go!

411
00:32:24,130 --> 00:32:25,548
‎-Is this it?
‎-Yeah.

412
00:32:27,759 --> 00:32:29,010
‎Come here.

413
00:32:29,093 --> 00:32:29,927
‎You got a death wish?

414
00:32:30,011 --> 00:32:31,345
‎Does this look like 100,000 won to you?

415
00:32:31,929 --> 00:32:33,514
‎But I gave it to you last week.

416
00:32:33,598 --> 00:32:35,099
‎That was the late fee, you idiot.

417
00:32:35,183 --> 00:32:36,642
‎Don't you know what that means?

418
00:32:36,726 --> 00:32:39,604
‎What late fee? I didn't borrow any money.

419
00:32:41,481 --> 00:32:42,857
‎He keeps talking back to us.

420
00:32:43,524 --> 00:32:45,318
‎-We've been going easy on you, huh?
‎-No.

421
00:32:45,401 --> 00:32:49,072
‎If you take 46,000 won out of 100,000 won,
‎you have 54,000 won left, right?

422
00:32:49,155 --> 00:32:50,573
‎Let's make it 1,000 won a hit.

423
00:32:50,656 --> 00:32:51,574
‎Let me off this time.

424
00:32:51,657 --> 00:32:54,118
‎I'll bring it tomorrow,
‎even if I have to steal it.

425
00:32:54,202 --> 00:32:55,703
‎Why do I have to let you off?

426
00:32:55,787 --> 00:32:57,580
‎Hey, kids.

427
00:32:57,663 --> 00:32:59,332
‎Which class is Kim Min-ji in?

428
00:32:59,415 --> 00:33:00,541
‎Who are you?

429
00:33:01,125 --> 00:33:03,127
‎Mister, we're busy right now.

430
00:33:03,211 --> 00:33:04,337
‎So get lost.

431
00:33:04,420 --> 00:33:06,172
‎Keep moving, or you'll get hurt.

432
00:33:10,259 --> 00:33:13,262
‎I know Kim Min-ji.
‎We're in the same class.

433
00:33:15,723 --> 00:33:17,266
‎I told you to get lost.

434
00:33:17,350 --> 00:33:18,392
‎What's wrong with the bastard?

435
00:33:18,476 --> 00:33:20,937
‎-You want to fight?
‎-I said get lost.

436
00:33:26,067 --> 00:33:27,610
‎Go get Kim Min-ji.

437
00:33:27,693 --> 00:33:30,071
‎She's not at school
‎because she was suspended.

438
00:33:30,613 --> 00:33:31,739
‎Call her.

439
00:33:31,823 --> 00:33:33,825
‎I don't know her number.

440
00:33:35,201 --> 00:33:37,203
‎But you can ask Kang Hye-ryeong.

441
00:33:37,787 --> 00:33:39,997
‎They're best friends,
‎so she can use Find Friends.

442
00:33:40,623 --> 00:33:42,166
‎What? "Find Friends"?

443
00:33:42,250 --> 00:33:46,003
‎Yes, you can check your friend's location
‎with your phone.

444
00:33:51,092 --> 00:33:52,510
‎Where is she right now?

445
00:33:55,429 --> 00:33:57,682
‎Min-ji has been suspended since yesterday.

446
00:33:57,765 --> 00:33:59,559
‎-Suspended?
‎-Yes.

447
00:34:00,184 --> 00:34:03,020
‎She violated some school policies.

448
00:34:04,397 --> 00:34:05,523
‎Sorry, one more thing.

449
00:34:05,606 --> 00:34:08,526
‎I heard her father came here
‎a few days ago.

450
00:34:08,609 --> 00:34:10,862
‎Was there a school violence incident?

451
00:34:12,613 --> 00:34:14,407
‎Goodness, school violence?

452
00:34:14,490 --> 00:34:16,159
‎You can't be serious.

453
00:34:16,242 --> 00:34:18,703
‎It was nothing of the sort.
‎Where did you hear such a rumor?

454
00:34:20,580 --> 00:34:21,497
‎There's no such thing

455
00:34:21,581 --> 00:34:24,834
‎as school violence or bullying
‎at our school.

456
00:34:25,459 --> 00:34:26,460
‎No such thing.

457
00:34:28,921 --> 00:34:31,132
‎I have to get going for class now.

458
00:34:31,215 --> 00:34:33,092
‎Feel free to talk to the others
‎if you'd like.

459
00:35:00,661 --> 00:35:01,495
‎Kang Hye-ryeong.

460
00:35:01,579 --> 00:35:04,999
‎Your fingers look pretty busy
‎for someone with a headache.

461
00:35:05,082 --> 00:35:07,460
‎I'm looking up ways
‎to get rid of my headache.

462
00:35:09,045 --> 00:35:10,379
‎At least your mouth is in perfect health.

463
00:35:11,088 --> 00:35:11,964
‎Let's go.

464
00:35:12,048 --> 00:35:12,882
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

465
00:35:34,278 --> 00:35:35,529
‎KANG HYE-RYEONG

466
00:35:36,906 --> 00:35:39,283
‎I swear I'm still not feeling well.

467
00:35:42,536 --> 00:35:43,496
‎Are you Kang Hye-ryeong?

468
00:35:46,165 --> 00:35:48,626
‎They say you can locate friends with this.

469
00:35:49,919 --> 00:35:51,045
‎You can do that, right?

470
00:36:04,767 --> 00:36:05,810
‎Jeez, you scared me.

471
00:36:05,893 --> 00:36:07,520
‎I almost had a heart attack.

472
00:36:07,603 --> 00:36:08,854
‎How long have you been here?

473
00:36:09,480 --> 00:36:12,817
‎For a while. I was waiting outside,
‎but it got too cold.

474
00:36:12,900 --> 00:36:14,819
‎You should've called ahead.

475
00:36:15,486 --> 00:36:18,072
‎They reassigned the surveillance team
‎to tracking detail.

476
00:36:18,155 --> 00:36:19,240
‎Any leads?

477
00:36:19,323 --> 00:36:21,409
‎I think the reason Agent Kim
‎went off the rails

478
00:36:21,492 --> 00:36:23,077
‎has something to do with his daughter.

479
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:24,996
‎Right, so that means

480
00:36:25,079 --> 00:36:28,124
‎we'll find him wherever his daughter is.

481
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:31,419
‎Why are you talking like that?

482
00:36:33,212 --> 00:36:35,923
‎I just wanted to have a little fun, okay?

483
00:36:36,007 --> 00:36:39,093
‎I've been working at the dry cleaners
‎for so long

484
00:36:39,176 --> 00:36:42,555
‎that I can't tell if I'm an SMD agent
‎or the owner of that place.

485
00:36:42,638 --> 00:36:45,266
‎I'm having an identity crisis.

486
00:36:45,891 --> 00:36:48,227
‎I guess you were cut out
‎for the laundry business.

487
00:36:48,311 --> 00:36:49,478
‎It could be your calling.

488
00:36:50,730 --> 00:36:53,065
‎Did you pick up any clues
‎in the neighborhood?

489
00:36:55,151 --> 00:36:55,985
‎No, not yet.

490
00:36:59,447 --> 00:37:00,865
‎Wow, that's cutting-edge.

491
00:37:06,912 --> 00:37:08,414
‎Times sure have changed.

492
00:37:43,574 --> 00:37:45,368
‎This abalone is rather tough.

493
00:37:46,744 --> 00:37:47,787
‎This place isn't great.

494
00:37:48,412 --> 00:37:49,246
‎Don't you agree?

495
00:37:49,830 --> 00:37:51,957
‎You must have a reason
‎for reaching out so suddenly.

496
00:37:57,338 --> 00:37:59,673
‎I cleared out the other rooms,
‎so you can talk freely.

497
00:38:05,179 --> 00:38:08,140
‎It's such a massive project

498
00:38:08,224 --> 00:38:10,518
‎that I'm not sure how to explain this.

499
00:38:13,270 --> 00:38:14,480
‎I guess you could say

500
00:38:15,147 --> 00:38:18,359
‎it's like building an entire city
‎out in the wasteland.

501
00:38:21,404 --> 00:38:24,990
‎I'm sure you saw on the news
‎that the high-level inter-Korean talks

502
00:38:25,074 --> 00:38:26,742
‎will take place soon.

503
00:38:26,826 --> 00:38:29,537
‎Do you know
‎what's at the top of the agenda?

504
00:38:33,541 --> 00:38:35,418
‎It's to establish a free-trade zone

505
00:38:35,501 --> 00:38:37,920
‎through a South-North joint venture.

506
00:38:39,713 --> 00:38:41,090
‎That's good news.

507
00:38:42,508 --> 00:38:45,302
‎We're in an era of peace now,
‎not confrontation.

508
00:38:46,429 --> 00:38:48,681
‎For a project of this scale,

509
00:38:48,764 --> 00:38:51,183
‎only a firm like Juhak Construction
‎can deliver.

510
00:38:51,851 --> 00:38:54,395
‎That's just my thought, but…

511
00:38:55,187 --> 00:38:56,021
‎Please continue.

512
00:38:58,315 --> 00:38:59,608
‎The thing is,

513
00:38:59,692 --> 00:39:02,403
‎I can't make this decision alone.

514
00:39:02,486 --> 00:39:05,364
‎I need a good reason
‎to convince the other assemblymen.

515
00:39:08,576 --> 00:39:11,370
‎Don't worry about the funding.
‎I'll provide whatever you need.

516
00:39:12,538 --> 00:39:16,000
‎Goodness, you put it so bluntly.

517
00:39:16,667 --> 00:39:18,919
‎I like that you and I
‎speak the same language.

518
00:39:20,504 --> 00:39:24,049
‎If a problem can't be solved with money,
‎it's because you don't have enough.

519
00:39:24,925 --> 00:39:25,926
‎And if it still doesn't work…

520
00:39:27,344 --> 00:39:28,179
‎If it doesn't?

521
00:39:30,306 --> 00:39:34,226
‎Just give me a list of the people
‎who can't be convinced.

522
00:40:10,012 --> 00:40:12,431
‎So Min-ji has disappeared somewhere…

523
00:40:15,142 --> 00:40:17,645
‎and her father is looking for her?

524
00:40:17,728 --> 00:40:20,439
‎We don't have a current location on him.

525
00:40:21,023 --> 00:40:22,066
‎We ran a background check,

526
00:40:22,149 --> 00:40:23,317
‎but access was denied.

527
00:40:24,568 --> 00:40:25,611
‎Something's off.

528
00:40:50,678 --> 00:40:51,929
‎Is this the place?

529
00:40:52,012 --> 00:40:53,597
‎Yeah, third floor.

530
00:40:55,266 --> 00:40:56,267
‎-Let's go.
‎-Okay.

531
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:19,665
‎Seriously, man.

532
00:41:21,542 --> 00:41:23,711
‎Jeez, there are so many of them.

533
00:41:27,172 --> 00:41:28,632
‎Hey, mister.

534
00:41:28,716 --> 00:41:30,926
‎You can't just walk in here. Please leave.

535
00:41:31,010 --> 00:41:32,261
‎How did they get in?

536
00:41:32,344 --> 00:41:34,388
‎Damn it. Hey, Taekwondo. Get out.

537
00:41:34,972 --> 00:41:36,765
‎-What's with the uniform?
‎-Darn it.

538
00:41:36,849 --> 00:41:39,435
‎I should've changed before coming.
‎I have lots of nice outfits.

539
00:41:40,477 --> 00:41:42,104
‎This might take some time.

540
00:41:42,896 --> 00:41:44,023
‎We don't have time.

541
00:41:44,106 --> 00:41:45,649
‎We'll push through the way they would.

542
00:41:45,733 --> 00:41:47,401
‎So you're going to play the thug, huh?

543
00:41:48,068 --> 00:41:49,403
‎Who's the head here?

544
00:41:49,486 --> 00:41:50,446
‎Is it you?

545
00:41:50,529 --> 00:41:51,530
‎What a joke.

546
00:41:53,824 --> 00:41:55,034
‎What head?

547
00:41:55,951 --> 00:41:56,785
‎Your blockhead?

548
00:41:58,329 --> 00:42:00,205
‎My guys told you to leave.

549
00:42:02,374 --> 00:42:03,375
‎Get lost.

550
00:42:04,835 --> 00:42:06,128
‎Let's just say it's you.

551
00:42:25,022 --> 00:42:26,774
‎Songin High School, Grade 11, Class 7.

552
00:42:27,483 --> 00:42:29,276
‎Brown jacket, yellow hoodie,

553
00:42:29,360 --> 00:42:30,653
‎a heart keychain on her phone.

554
00:42:30,736 --> 00:42:31,737
‎Has anyone seen her?

555
00:42:33,155 --> 00:42:34,156
‎No, sir.

556
00:42:34,239 --> 00:42:35,574
‎If not, then get out of my way.

557
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:37,743
‎Or else I'll skin you alive.

558
00:42:40,454 --> 00:42:41,413
‎Which way?

559
00:42:41,955 --> 00:42:42,956
‎That way.

560
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:50,756
‎-Wait.
‎-Damn it, he said not to let anyone in.

561
00:42:50,839 --> 00:42:52,132
‎Then go with them!

562
00:42:52,216 --> 00:42:53,467
‎You think I'm crazy?

563
00:42:53,550 --> 00:42:54,968
‎What are you all doing?

564
00:42:57,012 --> 00:42:58,722
‎I've got it here. You…

565
00:43:00,557 --> 00:43:03,519
‎I'm in this mess
‎because I have such good friends.

566
00:43:03,602 --> 00:43:07,064
‎-You need to choose your friends wisely.
‎-What's he talking about?

567
00:43:07,147 --> 00:43:08,190
‎Hey, get him!

568
00:43:48,230 --> 00:43:49,148
‎Boss.

569
00:43:49,732 --> 00:43:50,649
‎Someone's coming.

570
00:43:53,277 --> 00:43:55,446
‎I told you not to let any of the guys in.

571
00:43:59,908 --> 00:44:01,118
‎It's not one of our guys.

572
00:44:02,536 --> 00:44:03,579
‎It's some middle-aged guy.

573
00:44:04,371 --> 00:44:07,207
‎Who cares if it's a kid or a boomer?

574
00:44:14,465 --> 00:44:16,175
‎I told them to stay away, but they didn't.

575
00:44:16,967 --> 00:44:18,343
‎So now they're dead.

576
00:44:34,610 --> 00:44:37,613
‎Come on, I'm the queen of investing.

577
00:44:37,696 --> 00:44:40,657
‎Let's study investing together.
‎I'll send you a link.

578
00:44:40,741 --> 00:44:43,202
‎You want to meet up?
‎I'm a little busy this week.

579
00:44:43,869 --> 00:44:46,580
‎What are you talking about?
‎There's no one else but you.

580
00:44:47,873 --> 00:44:48,749
‎Hang on.

581
00:44:49,708 --> 00:44:52,252
‎Sir, he keeps saying he wants to meet up.

582
00:44:52,336 --> 00:44:53,670
‎How much did we get from him?

583
00:44:53,754 --> 00:44:55,881
‎About 30 million won this time.

584
00:44:57,758 --> 00:44:59,718
‎Just play it off. Say you're traveling.

585
00:45:00,302 --> 00:45:02,638
‎Jeez, I can't do this crap anymore.

586
00:45:02,721 --> 00:45:03,555
‎Hey.

587
00:45:04,181 --> 00:45:05,015
‎What the hell?

588
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:17,611
‎Just leave quietly.

589
00:45:17,694 --> 00:45:18,529
‎Move.

590
00:45:18,612 --> 00:45:20,614
‎Didn't you hear what the boss said?

591
00:45:20,697 --> 00:45:21,657
‎Sir.

592
00:45:22,241 --> 00:45:24,034
‎It's not like that.
‎This bastard suddenly--

593
00:45:28,205 --> 00:45:29,122
‎So you know how to box.

594
00:45:29,206 --> 00:45:30,916
‎I'll pop your eyes and eardrums.

595
00:45:31,917 --> 00:45:33,669
‎I'm different from the punks out there.

596
00:45:33,752 --> 00:45:35,337
‎You're just a punk who knows how to box.

597
00:45:53,605 --> 00:45:54,856
‎He's going to kill him.

598
00:45:55,649 --> 00:45:57,150
‎Someone go and stop Hyeong-min.

599
00:45:57,234 --> 00:46:00,320
‎I think that's Hyeong-min's voice.

600
00:46:09,454 --> 00:46:10,872
‎Who's that old man?

601
00:46:11,623 --> 00:46:12,749
‎Are you a cop?

602
00:46:15,669 --> 00:46:17,921
‎You think a knife won't go through a cop?

603
00:46:19,089 --> 00:46:21,508
‎They're all lumps of flesh in the end.

604
00:46:32,269 --> 00:46:33,395
‎Hey, mister.

605
00:46:34,062 --> 00:46:36,231
‎Didn't they tell you to stay out?

606
00:46:48,827 --> 00:46:50,162
‎Hey, take him down.

607
00:47:42,089 --> 00:47:43,590
‎Who wants another beating?

608
00:47:45,300 --> 00:47:46,468
‎No takers? Then get out.

609
00:47:46,551 --> 00:47:47,552
‎Get out!

610
00:47:52,057 --> 00:47:53,225
‎Jeez, my knees.

611
00:48:17,207 --> 00:48:19,251
‎Wow, that was amazing.

612
00:48:19,334 --> 00:48:20,377
‎You're so cool.

613
00:48:22,587 --> 00:48:24,506
‎Do you run a mobile phone store?

614
00:48:28,385 --> 00:48:31,138
‎Where did you get that phone?

615
00:48:32,431 --> 00:48:33,265
‎What do you mean?

616
00:48:35,434 --> 00:48:37,144
‎Oh, this?

617
00:48:37,769 --> 00:48:39,688
‎Where did I get this from again?

618
00:48:41,356 --> 00:48:42,190
‎Hold on.

619
00:48:43,108 --> 00:48:44,151
‎Let me check the photo.

620
00:48:52,367 --> 00:48:54,578
‎Darn, I feel like I should remember.

621
00:48:59,583 --> 00:49:00,417
‎Oh, I know.

622
00:49:03,086 --> 00:49:06,047
‎It's the girl
‎I messed around with last night.

623
00:51:01,872 --> 00:51:02,789
‎Kim!

624
00:51:06,251 --> 00:51:07,502
‎Are you going to kill him?

625
00:51:08,420 --> 00:51:10,422
‎We need to ask him where Min-ji is.

626
00:51:17,804 --> 00:51:19,514
‎Think carefully before you answer.

627
00:51:20,015 --> 00:51:21,933
‎Do you know who Kim Min-ji is?

628
00:51:22,475 --> 00:51:23,393
‎I don't.

629
00:51:25,103 --> 00:51:26,855
‎I've never seen her before.

630
00:51:28,064 --> 00:51:29,357
‎I swear!

631
00:51:34,321 --> 00:51:35,322
‎Then tell me.

632
00:51:36,031 --> 00:51:37,157
‎Where did you get this from?

633
00:51:39,951 --> 00:51:40,827
‎The thing is…

634
00:51:42,078 --> 00:51:43,371
‎Damn.

635
00:51:44,998 --> 00:51:46,750
‎That's a nice phone. How about this?

636
00:51:47,459 --> 00:51:48,293
‎Ta-da.

637
00:51:48,919 --> 00:51:49,920
‎Want to trade?

638
00:51:51,171 --> 00:51:52,589
‎-Hello, sir.
‎-Hello.

639
00:51:52,672 --> 00:51:54,549
‎-Show us your haul.
‎-On the table.

640
00:51:56,301 --> 00:51:57,594
‎Be gentle, man.

641
00:51:58,637 --> 00:51:59,638
‎Did you unlock them?

642
00:51:59,721 --> 00:52:02,349
‎Yes, we unlocked the ones
‎to sell as burners.

643
00:52:02,432 --> 00:52:04,809
‎And I told the guys
‎to fix the ones with cracked screens.

644
00:52:05,310 --> 00:52:06,311
‎Hyeong-min.

645
00:52:07,354 --> 00:52:08,355
‎Any girls' phones?

646
00:52:09,397 --> 00:52:11,983
‎Are there any with sexy bikini photos?

647
00:52:20,116 --> 00:52:22,494
‎I have a good feeling about this.

648
00:52:22,577 --> 00:52:24,037
‎I think she'll be pretty.

649
00:52:24,120 --> 00:52:24,955
‎Let me see.

650
00:52:26,623 --> 00:52:27,624
‎Oh, look at that.

651
00:52:27,707 --> 00:52:28,708
‎She's pretty cute.

652
00:52:34,464 --> 00:52:35,382
‎This is it?

653
00:52:36,341 --> 00:52:37,759
‎How boring.

654
00:52:38,385 --> 00:52:39,260
‎Keep going.

655
00:52:42,097 --> 00:52:43,974
‎DAD

656
00:52:44,057 --> 00:52:45,100
‎I knew it.

657
00:52:45,642 --> 00:52:47,894
‎Her dad is the only one
‎in her call history.

658
00:52:47,978 --> 00:52:49,646
‎I guess she only has her dad.

659
00:52:50,563 --> 00:52:51,731
‎Hey.

660
00:52:51,815 --> 00:52:53,233
‎Bring me another one.

661
00:52:53,316 --> 00:52:54,234
<i>‎Hello?</i>

662
00:52:55,318 --> 00:52:56,778
<i>‎-Is that you, Min-ji?</i>
‎-What the hell?

663
00:52:56,861 --> 00:52:58,071
‎Damn it, I pressed the wrong button.

664
00:52:58,154 --> 00:52:59,781
‎DAD

665
00:52:59,864 --> 00:53:03,118
‎So I turned off the phone right away.

666
00:53:03,201 --> 00:53:04,327
‎Hold on.

667
00:53:05,245 --> 00:53:06,246
‎What did you just say?

668
00:53:06,329 --> 00:53:07,330
‎I turned off the phone.

669
00:53:07,414 --> 00:53:08,248
‎No.

670
00:53:08,873 --> 00:53:09,874
‎Before that.

671
00:53:10,583 --> 00:53:11,793
‎About the call history.

672
00:53:11,876 --> 00:53:14,004
‎I only saw "Dad" in it.

673
00:53:14,713 --> 00:53:16,297
‎There wasn't a single friend.

674
00:53:17,841 --> 00:53:18,675
‎Oh.

675
00:53:19,467 --> 00:53:21,928
‎HYE-RYEONG

676
00:53:22,012 --> 00:53:23,054
‎There was one.

677
00:53:25,515 --> 00:53:26,349
<i>‎Kang Hye-ryeong.</i>

678
00:53:26,433 --> 00:53:28,435
‎I need the name of a close friend

679
00:53:28,518 --> 00:53:29,894
‎and their phone number.

680
00:53:32,022 --> 00:53:33,982
‎-Kim Min-ji!
‎-Kang Hye-ryeong.

681
00:53:34,065 --> 00:53:36,568
‎Her number is 010-0610-6003.

682
00:53:36,651 --> 00:53:40,113
‎I'm staying at Hye-ryeong's tonight,
‎so don't call me.

683
00:53:41,906 --> 00:53:42,741
‎But I don't know

684
00:53:43,366 --> 00:53:45,035
‎if I'd call her a friend.

685
00:53:46,286 --> 00:53:48,204
<i>‎Min-ji, can I borrow 20,000 won?</i>

686
00:53:48,288 --> 00:53:49,539
<i>‎Can you lend me your phone?</i>

687
00:53:49,622 --> 00:53:50,457
‎Lend me your phone.

688
00:53:50,540 --> 00:53:51,708
‎What's with the crappy phone?

689
00:53:51,791 --> 00:53:52,876
‎Lend me your gym clothes.

690
00:53:52,959 --> 00:53:53,793
‎Thank you.

691
00:53:53,877 --> 00:53:56,046
<i>‎Sorry, I lost your gym clothes.</i>

692
00:53:56,129 --> 00:53:58,131
<i>‎It's my birthday tomorrow.</i>
<i>‎Can you buy me foundation?</i>

693
00:53:59,174 --> 00:54:00,008
‎It looked like…

694
00:54:01,342 --> 00:54:03,470
‎she was just using her.

695
00:54:06,973 --> 00:54:09,225
<i>‎I had no idea.</i>

696
00:54:09,309 --> 00:54:12,896
<i>‎I pray</i>

697
00:54:12,979 --> 00:54:16,149
<i>‎For you</i>

698
00:54:16,232 --> 00:54:19,944
<i>‎I pray</i>

699
00:54:20,028 --> 00:54:23,782
<i>‎You'll be protected</i>

700
00:54:23,865 --> 00:54:28,369
<i>‎So that my hopes reach you--</i>

701
00:54:29,537 --> 00:54:30,371
‎Kim Min-ji.

702
00:54:30,455 --> 00:54:33,249
‎At least help me clean
‎if you're staying home on the weekend.

703
00:54:33,333 --> 00:54:34,918
‎Why are you holed up in your room?

704
00:54:35,418 --> 00:54:36,836
‎Go hang out with your friends instead.

705
00:54:36,920 --> 00:54:38,671
‎It's hot outside.

706
00:54:38,755 --> 00:54:40,006
‎It's hot in your room too.

707
00:54:42,050 --> 00:54:43,301
‎Take this and come out.

708
00:55:01,820 --> 00:55:03,404
‎I didn't do anything wrong.

709
00:55:04,114 --> 00:55:06,116
‎She and her girls kept harassing me.

710
00:55:06,658 --> 00:55:08,743
‎I took it for as long as I could
‎before fighting back!

711
00:55:08,827 --> 00:55:09,786
‎Kim Min-ji.

712
00:55:10,620 --> 00:55:11,454
‎Be quiet.

713
00:55:13,915 --> 00:55:15,458
‎Jeez, wash your clothes.

714
00:55:17,752 --> 00:55:19,212
‎I said don't look at me like that!

715
00:55:19,712 --> 00:55:21,005
‎That's enough.

716
00:55:22,423 --> 00:55:25,218
‎Stop picking on that pathetic kid.

717
00:55:29,389 --> 00:55:30,223
‎Come out.

718
00:55:41,693 --> 00:55:42,694
<i>‎Why?</i>

719
00:55:44,529 --> 00:55:46,406
<i>‎Why didn't I notice sooner?</i>

720
00:55:50,577 --> 00:55:51,411
‎Hey.

721
00:55:51,953 --> 00:55:53,079
‎Get it together.

722
00:55:53,830 --> 00:55:55,540
‎There's no time to get emotional.

723
00:55:58,251 --> 00:56:00,420
‎It must've been so hard for her.

724
00:56:01,421 --> 00:56:02,338
‎My poor Min-ji…

725
00:56:03,715 --> 00:56:05,008
‎I know you've tried hard.

726
00:56:05,967 --> 00:56:07,594
‎And I know you're hurting a lot.

727
00:56:09,304 --> 00:56:10,388
‎Han-soo.

728
00:56:10,471 --> 00:56:11,723
‎But you're her dad.

729
00:56:13,558 --> 00:56:15,393
‎So let's find Min-ji first.

730
00:56:15,894 --> 00:56:17,812
‎You can't apologize unless you do.

731
00:56:32,577 --> 00:56:33,453
‎So?

732
00:56:34,120 --> 00:56:35,371
‎Where did you get this again?

733
00:56:35,455 --> 00:56:36,331
‎Sorry?

734
00:56:36,998 --> 00:56:38,583
‎At Hwasin Station.

735
00:56:39,709 --> 00:56:41,502
‎I took it from a homeless man.

736
00:56:43,379 --> 00:56:44,380
‎Let's go.

737
00:56:51,721 --> 00:56:53,306
‎Here you are.

738
00:57:03,149 --> 00:57:04,817
‎Fake 66.

739
00:57:17,997 --> 00:57:20,917
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

740
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:27,799
‎EPILOGUE

741
00:57:45,483 --> 00:57:46,484
‎Name?

742
00:57:50,154 --> 00:57:51,030
‎Age?

743
00:57:54,784 --> 00:57:56,452
‎Family?

744
00:57:58,580 --> 00:58:00,164
‎Right.

745
00:58:00,248 --> 00:58:03,543
‎What's the point of any of this?

746
00:58:03,626 --> 00:58:09,048
‎Your name and identity
‎are all a secret anyway, right?

747
00:58:10,508 --> 00:58:12,594
‎Why are you keeping me alive?

748
00:58:12,677 --> 00:58:14,887
‎That's a good question.

749
00:58:15,805 --> 00:58:16,889
‎Well, let's see.

750
00:58:16,973 --> 00:58:20,810
‎Killing you won't speed up reunification.

751
00:58:21,519 --> 00:58:23,146
‎And depending on the situation,

752
00:58:23,229 --> 00:58:25,898
‎we might be able to help each other out.

753
00:58:26,566 --> 00:58:28,067
‎I have this feeling

754
00:58:28,735 --> 00:58:32,488
‎that you could be
‎of some sort of help to us.

755
00:58:32,572 --> 00:58:33,573
‎Yeah, a gut feeling.

756
00:58:34,157 --> 00:58:36,159
‎Are you asking me to betray my homeland?

757
00:58:36,993 --> 00:58:38,828
‎Goodness.

758
00:58:38,911 --> 00:58:42,832
‎How can a man with no name, age, or family

759
00:58:42,915 --> 00:58:44,292
‎have a homeland?

760
00:58:52,383 --> 00:58:55,011
‎Here comes the guy
‎who hunts down people like you.

761
00:58:55,762 --> 00:58:56,596
‎Come in.

762
00:59:02,226 --> 00:59:04,145
‎Goodness.

763
00:59:04,228 --> 00:59:06,731
‎Look who's here to grace this fine place
‎with their lowly presence.

764
00:59:06,814 --> 00:59:08,608
‎It's Park Jin-cheol.

765
00:59:09,192 --> 00:59:10,068
‎Life or death.

766
00:59:10,777 --> 00:59:11,653
‎Fight to the end!

767
00:59:16,699 --> 00:59:18,034
‎From up north

768
00:59:19,243 --> 00:59:20,328
‎and down south.

769
00:59:21,412 --> 00:59:22,538
‎Go on.

770
00:59:23,289 --> 00:59:24,582
‎Greet your fellow top dog.

771
00:59:25,375 --> 00:59:26,250
‎Is this that buddy?

772
00:59:26,334 --> 00:59:28,961
‎He's not quite a buddy yet.

773
00:59:30,505 --> 00:59:31,839
‎Hey, comrade.

774
00:59:33,383 --> 00:59:36,636
‎Before we decide
‎whether you'll be our buddy or a commie,

775
00:59:37,512 --> 00:59:39,681
‎let's assess your skills first.

776
00:59:41,307 --> 00:59:42,684
‎Don't kill him just yet.

777
00:59:43,559 --> 00:59:45,812
‎A soldier either kills or gets killed.

778
01:00:04,372 --> 01:00:05,206
‎Don't hold back

779
01:00:06,624 --> 01:00:07,500
‎if you want to live.

780
01:00:09,752 --> 01:00:11,170
‎If I want to live?

781
01:00:13,756 --> 01:00:17,135
‎I have no desire to live.

782
01:00:18,803 --> 01:00:19,804
‎I'm just…

783
01:00:21,556 --> 01:00:24,308
‎keeping the promise I made
‎to my only friend.

784
01:00:27,437 --> 01:00:28,396
‎I like that.

785
01:00:32,483 --> 01:00:33,735
‎What's your name?

786
01:00:35,570 --> 01:00:36,529
‎It's 73.

787
01:00:37,447 --> 01:00:38,281
‎No.

788
01:00:42,744 --> 01:00:43,786
‎It's 66.

789
01:00:46,497 --> 01:00:47,790
‎Bring it on, 66.

790
01:01:37,298 --> 01:01:40,927
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

791
01:01:43,137 --> 01:01:46,140
<i>‎I expected someone would be watching me.</i>

792
01:01:47,558 --> 01:01:50,645
<i>‎If he doesn't want his precious daughter</i>
<i>‎to go to prison…</i>

793
01:01:50,728 --> 01:01:51,562
‎Crush him.

794
01:01:54,440 --> 01:01:55,775
‎Stop!

795
01:01:55,858 --> 01:01:57,151
‎What are you, a damn deer?!

796
01:01:58,277 --> 01:02:00,029
<i>‎You know whose phone this is, don't you?</i>

797
01:02:00,112 --> 01:02:01,823
<i>‎Did you check if she was dead?</i>

798
01:02:01,906 --> 01:02:03,074
<i>‎Promise me…</i>

799
01:02:04,826 --> 01:02:06,452
<i>‎you'll survive.</i>

800
01:02:06,536 --> 01:02:09,914
<i>‎I'll take good care of the body</i>
<i>‎in the meantime.</i>

801
01:02:12,959 --> 01:02:17,964
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

